  "textContent": "Filming for the television special James Paul McCartney continued on 12 March 1973 at Elstree Studios. This day’s filming was briefly interrupted due to a bomb scare, leading to the evacuation of the studios.Produced by ATV, James Paul McCartney was first broadcast on 16 April 1973 in the USA, and 10 May in the UK. It was released on DVD as part of the super deluxe reissue of in Red Rose Speedway December 2018.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 28 November 2025Also on this day...2026: Beatles memorabilia in Jim Irsay collection sells for over $17 million1999: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Dee Events Center, Ogden1975: Recording: Treat Her Gently/Lonely Old People by Wings1974: John Lennon watches the Smothers Brothers perform in Los Angeles1971: Recording: Dear Boy by Paul and Linda McCartney1971: Paul McCartney wins lawsuit to dissolve The Beatles’ partnership1971: UK single release: Power To The People by John Lennon1970: George and Pattie Harrison move into Friar Park1969: George and Pattie Harrison’s home is raided by the Drugs Squad1969: Paul McCartney marries Linda Eastman1969: Mixing: The Long And Winding Road, Let It Be1964: Filming: A Hard Day’s Night1963: The Beatles live: Granada Cinema, Bedford1962: The Beatles live: Kingsway Club, Southport1961: The Beatles live: Cassanova Club, Liverpool1961: The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
